    "## What is NumPy?\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 1 – Understand the Concept\n",
    "\n",
    "NumPy is a Python library for efficient numerical computing built around multidimensional arrays.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 2 – Demonstrate the Concept\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Simple example:** Think of it as a fast numerical workspace for vectors and matrices.\n",
    "- **Real-world analogy:** A spreadsheet column that only holds one kind of number, so every cell is handled the same fast way.\n",
    "- **Business example:** Sales analysts store daily revenue in arrays to sum and compare periods quickly.\n",
    "- **AI/ML example:** Image pixels, sensor readings and model weights are all stored as NumPy arrays.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each example represents the concept because it shows the same idea: apply the operation to many values or records in one consistent step."
   ]
  },
