    "## Why NumPy?\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 1 – Understand the Concept\n",
    "\n",
    "NumPy supports compact arrays and vectorized numerical operations.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 2 – Demonstrate the Concept\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Simple example:** Instead of processing each number manually, a whole feature vector can be transformed at once.\n",
    "- **Real-world analogy:** A calculator that applies one operation to a whole row of numbers at once instead of one by one.\n",
    "- **Business example:** Raising every price in a list by 5 without writing a loop.\n",
    "- **AI/ML example:** Scaling an entire feature column before training is one vectorized line.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each example represents the concept because it shows the same idea: apply the operation to many values or records in one consistent step."
   ]
