    "## Copy vs View\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 1 – Understand the Concept\n",
    "\n",
    "A view shares underlying data; a copy has independent data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 2 – Demonstrate the Concept\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Simple example:** Understanding this prevents accidental changes during preprocessing.\n",
    "- **Real-world analogy:** A view is a window onto the same garden; a copy is a photograph of it.\n",
    "- **Business example:** Editing a slice of a report accidentally changing the original data.\n",
    "- **AI/ML example:** Accidental changes through views can silently corrupt training data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each example represents the concept because it shows the same idea: apply the operation to many values or records in one consistent step."
   ]
  },
