   "source": [
    "## Best Practices\n",
    "\n",
    "- Choose an appropriate dtype and inspect arr.dtype before calculations.\n",
    "- Check arr.shape, arr.ndim, and arr.size before reshaping or combining arrays.\n",
    "- Prefer vectorized NumPy operations for element-wise calculations instead of unnecessary Python loops.\n",
    "- Use .copy() when you need an independent array; basic slices can share data with the original.\n",
    "- Verify sample values after array creation, slicing, or reshaping."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7a7539d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Common Mistakes\n",
    "\n",
    "- Confusing shape, size, and number of dimensions.\n",
    "- Reshaping an array to a shape with a different total number of elements.\n",
    "- Assuming a slice is always an independent copy when it may be a view.\n",
    "- Combining arrays with incompatible shapes without checking broadcasting.\n",
    "- Using lists for repeated numerical operations that are better handled by NumPy arrays."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1b268ad8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "- NumPy provides efficient multidimensional arrays for numerical data.\n",
    "- Vectorized operations reduce repetitive Python code for element-wise calculations.\n",
    "- Indexing, slicing, reshaping, and broadcasting support concise array transformations.\n",
    "- NumPy integrates with common scientific-computing and machine-learning libraries."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "db4d4601",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "- Arrays generally use one common dtype, which may not suit mixed-type records.\n",
    "- Broadcasting can produce unexpected results if dimensions are not checked.\n",
    "- Large arrays and unnecessary copies can consume significant memory.\n",
    "- NumPy arrays do not provide all the labeled-table conveniences of a Pandas DataFrame."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9fbe9f37",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Interview Questions with Answers\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q1. Why is NumPy important in AI/ML?**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** It provides efficient arrays and vectorized numerical operations used throughout data preparation and modeling.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q2. What is ndarray?**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** NumPy's multidimensional array object.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q3. What is broadcasting?**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** A mechanism for applying operations between compatible arrays with different shapes.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q4. Copy vs view?**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** A copy has independent data; a view generally shares the original data.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q5. Shape vs size?**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** Shape describes dimensions; size is the total number of elements."
   ]
  },
